{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfBT4hNuGx2GAPfQRQcYH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've submitted the Ni-V oxide campaign and picked **index 8 (Ni 0.29 / V 0.71)** as the best composition. It had the highest photocurrent I measured, 1.75 µA. I used all 3 merit measurements and 4 of the 5 XRD scans.\n\n| Index | Ni fraction | Photocurrent | What XRD showed |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 8 | 0.29 | **1.75 µA** | NiV₂O₆-type phase |\n| 12 | 0.34 | 1.42 µA | same phase |\n| 11 | 0.59 | 0.09 µA | no scan (Ni-rich side) |\n| 3 | 0.24 | not measured | same phase |\n| 0 | 0.13 | not measured | same phase plus a V₂O₅-like second phase |\n\n- **V-rich compositions win.** Moving to Ni 0.34 gave about 16 times more photocurrent than Ni 0.59, and Ni 0.29 was higher again.\n- **One crystal phase runs from Ni 0.24 to 0.34.** Below that, at Ni 0.13, a second phase appears. The best composition is probably inside the single-phase range.\n- **What's untested:** I ran out of merit measurements before trying index 3 (Ni 0.24). It sits in the same phase, so it could match or slightly beat index 8. It's the first one to measure if more budget becomes available."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":568,"cache_read_input_tokens":8693,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":568},"output_tokens":478,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b949c003-176b-462f-a1eb-c68aa8cbdb00","uuid":"06d89716-1da7-4879-a224-d71db777835e","timestamp":"2026-09-18T19:23:14.681Z","request_id":"req_011CfBT4grPzn6ghZat7Zmi9"}
